# Agent Shield Rules

## Shell Safety
- **pwsh 7** (Store version) is the default. NEVER use PowerShell 5.1 (`powershell.exe`).
- Write scripts to files, never inline cross-shell one-liners.
- `python -c` works (pass-through wrapper), but for multi-line Python use `py-run $code` or script files.
- `bash -c` works (pass-through wrapper), but for complex bash use `.sh` script files.
- NEVER nest single quotes in inline PowerShell.

## Encoding
- UTF-8 is set automatically by `agent-init.ps1` (Console, OutputEncoding, PYTHONIOENCODING, chcp 65001).
- Do NOT use registry ACP fix — it crashes Electron apps.

## Process Management
- Run `mem-optimize` before heavy operations to kill memory wastes and set priorities.
- Run `ports` before starting servers to check for conflicts.
- Kill what you spawn — clean up processes after use.
- Qoder/node = AboveNormal priority. explorer/Telegram/chrome = BelowNormal.

## SSH
- `ControlMaster no` — Windows OpenSSH does NOT support Unix domain sockets.
- Mac SSH: `ssh mac` (root). Non-interactive needs `bash -l -c` for PATH.
- Use `ssh-run -Host <ip> -Command <cmd>` to avoid escaping issues.

## Command Deny List
Never execute directly: `rm`, `mv`, `sudo`, `wget`, `curl`, `chown`.
Use PowerShell equivalents or agent-safe wrappers.
